{
  "_comment": [
    "Differential pin for the TWO canonicalizer implementations (issue #1455).",
    "",
    "canonical.py and canonical.mjs are independent implementations of one",
    "written spec. Two implementations are only KNOWN to agree if something",
    "checks; this table is that check. Every vector is materialized into each",
    "leg's NATIVE value shape and canonicalized by that leg's adapter; all",
    "three must produce `canonical` exactly.",
    "",
    "Leg value encoding: plain JSON where the native type is already JSON",
    "(bool/number/string/null); otherwise a tagged object materialized by",
    "vectors.py / vectors.mjs:",
    "  {\"$\":\"uuid\"|\"decimal\"|\"inet\"|\"bigint\"|\"date\", \"v\": ...}",
    "  {\"$\":\"bytes\", \"hex\": ...}   {\"$\":\"datetime\", \"ms\": ...}",
    "  {\"$\":\"duration\", \"months\":..., \"days\":..., \"nanos\": \"...\"}",
    "  {\"$\":\"list\"|\"set\"|\"tuple\", \"items\": [...]}",
    "  {\"$\":\"map\", \"entries\": [[k, v], ...]}",
    "The `cli` leg needs no tags -- its values are already parsed JSON.",
    "",
    "A `cli` value of null means 'this shape is unreachable from the CLI'; the",
    "vector then pins only the python and node legs. That is used ONLY for a",
    "value the CLI cannot emit, never to excuse a divergence."
  ],
